      "sourceCount": 2,
      "answer": "SHA-256: `a9642da7ebb756f1b0e0c15578b576e30f75fd542ab6fbb0d4702a3da18dcde4`\n\nReview: `open_go_client` keeps managed proxy/CA behavior by leaving `transport=None`, so `trust_env=True` preserves environment proxy mounts, NO_PROXY, and CA settings [S1]. Destinations are bounded at request time by `_go_destination`, allowing only HTTPS `opencode.ai` on port 443/None with no userinfo, query, fragment, `@`, or `#` [S1]. Redirects are disabled (`follow_redirects=False`), and default retries are 0 [S1]. Tested: proxy failure yields one proxied attempt, no direct fallback, no retry [S2]. Suggestions: keep these invariants covered when transport is injected.",
